# This Unarian program takes input n and computes n^2.
# 
# While this would be a simple task in common programming languages, it's much
# more difficult in Unarian, since there's only one accessible integer at any
# point in the execution of the program. As far as I can tell, computing
# squares requires being able to store multiple integers in memory. This means
# that it's necessary to design functions for encode and decoding values from
# 'virtual' integers (also called registers) stored in a single integer. Most
# of the complexity of this program comes from these functions.
# 
# The strategy for storing virtual integers is to interlace the bits of two
# integers together. For example, we can store 0b101 and 0b10110 by: spacing
# out their bits: 0b1_0_1 and 0b1_0_1_1_0; shifting one of them up: 0b1_0_1_
# and 0b1_0_1_1_0; bitwise combining the results together: 0b1_0110110; and
# filling the gaps 0b100110110. It's not hard to see that this process is
# reversible and can be used to retrieve any one of the stored integers.

#==================#
# Basic Operations #
#==================#

# Outputs 0.
0 { - 0 | }

# Continues if input is 0. Fails otherwise.
if=0 { { - 0 | + } - }

# Continues if input is not 0. Fails otherwise.
if>0 { - + }



#============#
# Arithmetic #
#============#

# Adds 4.
+4 { + + + + }

# Subtracts 4.
-4 { - - - - }

# Multiplies by 4.
<< { - << +4 | }

# Divides by 4 (floored division).
>> { -4 >> + | 0 }

# Adds to least significant digits
+00 { }
+01 { + }
+10 { + + }
+11 { + + + }

# Subtracts from least significant digits
-00 { }
-01 { - }
-10 { - - }
-11 { - - - }

# Checks least significant digits
if=00mod4 { -4 if=00mod4 +4 | if=0 }
if=01mod4 { -01 if=00mod4 +01 }
if=10mod4 { -10 if=00mod4 +10 }
if=11mod4 { -11 if=00mod4 +11 }



#=====================#
# Register Operations #
#=====================#

# Increment register A/B
A++ { if=10mod4 >> A++ << +00 | if=11mod4 >> A++ << +01 | +10 }
B++ { if=01mod4 >> B++ << +00 | if=11mod4 >> B++ << +10 | +01 }

# Decrement register A/B
A-- { if>0 if=00mod4 >> A-- << +10 | if=01mod4 >> A-- << +11 | if=10mod4 -10 | if=11mod4 -10 }
B-- { if>0 if=00mod4 >> B-- << +01 | if=10mod4 >> B-- << +11 | if=01mod4 -01 | if=11mod4 -01 }

# Set register A/B to current value
setA { - setA A++ | 0 }
setB { - setB B++ | 0 }

# Get value of register A/B
getA { A-- getA + | 0 }
getB { B-- getB + | 0 }



#==========#
# Squaring #
#==========#

A+=2B { B-- A++ A++ A+=2B B++ | }

A+=B^2 { B-- A++ A+=2B A+=B^2 | }

square { setB A+=B^2 getA }

main { square }

